        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In Firefox 147, when pseudo-element nodes are selected in the HTML pane of the Inspector — for example, those representing generated content created by <code class=\"notranslate\">::before</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">::after</code> rules — you can now edit the selectors of the corresponding rules in the Rule view. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998704\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998704</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42316",
            "title": "Fx147 devtools edit pseudo element selector",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T14:39:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T14:37:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 supports brotli compression in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CompressionStream/CompressionStream\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">CompressionStream</code> constructor</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DecompressionStream/DecompressionStream\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">DecompressionStream()</code> constructor</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1921583\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1921583</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note. It also updates the two constructors to include the brotli option and zstd option (which is also supported).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699242115\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42251\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42251/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42251\">#42251</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42312",
            "title": "FF147 Relnote: CompressionStream/DecompressionStream support brotli +…",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:23:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T06:30:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3708656574\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42306\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42306/hovercard?comment_id=3629944371&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306#issuecomment-3629944371\">#42306 (comment)</a> the description of import assertions does not provide an easy way to link to particular parts of the concepts, such as a definition of CSS Modules imported using <code class=\"notranslate\">with { type: \"css\"}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This restructures the existing material to provide some headings. Should allow clean linking to the doc, easier parsing for readers, and maintenance if we later add other module types.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Josh-Cena\">@Josh-Cena</a> Obviously \"for discussion and iteration\". It is almost all a restructure, with only a tiny amount of new content, which I will highlight.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work being done in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699248949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42255/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\">#42255</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42309",
            "title": "Restructure import assertions description to ease maintainability",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:21:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T05:26:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 adds support for module scripts in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681</a>. This allows you to do stuff like below to import a stylesheet and adopt it into your document.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"import sheet from './styles.css' with { type: 'css' };\ndocument.adoptedStyleSheets = [sheet];\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sheet</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'./styles.css'</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">with</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>: <span class=\"pl-s\">'css'</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">adoptedStyleSheets</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">sheet</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699248949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42255/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\">#42255</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306",
            "title": "FF147 Relnote: CSS Module scripts",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T02:36:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T00:59:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 implements module service workers in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1360870\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1360870</a>. This adds the release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can bet tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699239325\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42249\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42249/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42249\">#42249</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42304",
            "title": "FF147 Relnote: Module service workers",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T08:21:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T00:08:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #38229.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2862878729\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38229\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/38229/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38229\">#38229</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigation/reload\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Navigation.reload()</code></a> reloads the current page - a soft navigation because data is not fetched from the server. This change adds a note that this action does not fire the <code class=\"notranslate\">popstate</code> event.<br>\n<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/noamr/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/noamr\">@noamr</a> Points out that it does fire for other soft navigations, so people might expect it to fire for this one.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I \"weakly\" disagree. If you look at the documentation of <code class=\"notranslate\">popstate</code> it pretty clearly requires a modification to the history stack, which this does not cause. That said, I'm not an expert, and I don't think this does harm.<br>\nIf the reviewer rejects this I will not be unhappy.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is part of work for <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699247245\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42254\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42254/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42254\">#42254</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42303",
            "title": "Navigation.reload() does not trigger popstate event",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T09:28:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-08T23:14:20.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7843391?u=9efe83d5b512e6fc0848eee0337664922da2311d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the description of the AudioBufferSourceNode <code class=\"notranslate\">start()</code>'s <code class=\"notranslate\">duration</code> parameter so it's not said to be similar to calling <code class=\"notranslate\">stop(duration)</code>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Since this specs change <a href=\"https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/pull/1681\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebAudio/web-audio-api/pull/1681/hovercard\">1</a> (in 2018) the <code class=\"notranslate\">duration</code> argument is specced <a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#dom-audiobuffersourcenode-start-when-offset-duration-duration\" rel=\"nofollow\">2</a> as being the duration of the buffer's content to be played, and not necessarily the one of the AudioContext's clock. So if the source node has a <code class=\"notranslate\">playbackRate</code> that is not <code class=\"notranslate\">1</code>, using this parameter will not be the same as using <code class=\"notranslate\">stop(duration)</code>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I based the wordings on the specs text, but I don't mind another formulation altogether.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Might also be noted that there is an interop issue here, where only Firefox does follow the specs. I'll open issues to get this sorted out though.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"334611177\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/1681\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebAudio/web-audio-api/pull/1681/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/pull/1681\">WebAudio/web-audio-api#1681</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#dom-audiobuffersourcenode-start-when-offset-duration-duration\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#dom-audiobuffersourcenode-start-when-offset-duration-duration</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42282",
            "title": "Fix ABSN.start()'s 'duration' parameter description",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T01:18:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-08T08:07:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Kaiido",
                "url": "https://github.com/Kaiido"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83744975?u=2ad0feaa0569c5bde842b07ada630a9f10eab41f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">unmarked not required aria attributes as required.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Because <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-selected</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">option</code> role and <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-valuenow</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">spinbutton</code> role are not required and both roles have default values for their attributes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#spinbutton\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#spinbutton</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Authors SHOULD set the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#aria-valuenow\" rel=\"nofollow\">aria-valuenow</a> attribute when the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#spinbutton\" rel=\"nofollow\">spinbutton</a> has a value.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(-&gt;not <strong>MUST</strong>)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Default for <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#aria-valuenow\" rel=\"nofollow\">aria-valuenow</a> is 0</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#option\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#option</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Elements with the role option have an implicit <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#aria-selected\" rel=\"nofollow\">aria-selected</a> value of false.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Default for <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#aria-selected\" rel=\"nofollow\">aria-selected</a> is false.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42276",
            "title": "fix: not mark required aria attributes as required",
